  "strategy": "1. Approach and Rationale:\nA hybrid genetic multi-resolution framework: \n- Explores binary (fractional) representations of h(x)\n- Uses a two-population hybrid for non-uniform discoveries\n- Implements multi-stage adaptive factors for search control\n- Introduces early termination and restart on introduced diversity\nKey innovations:\n  1. Resolution mixing with predicted fitness trends\n  2. Dynamic generation sharing based on quality-vs-expense tradeoffs\n  3. Sophisticated repair schedules tied to lag dependencies\n  4. Candidate measurement specifically of overlap reduction across all shifts\nAddresses:\n  - Non-convex optimization complexity\n  - Difficulty proving equivalence in mixed representations\n  - Need for alignment with original correlation metric\n  - Risk of premature convergence\n\n2. Mathematical Specification:\nRepresentation:\n  - n_points: [95,200,400] (flexible)\n  - dx = 2.0 / n_points\nConstraints:\n  (1) \u2200i: 0 \u2264 h[i] \u2264 1\n  (2) sum(h) \u2248 n_points/2\nObjective:\n  C5 = max_k { \u222b h(x)(1-h(x+k)) dx } equivalent to:\n      max(np.correlate(h,1-h,mode='full') * dx\nVariables:\n  h: n-points vector from 0 to 1\nParameters:\n  MAX_TIME = 1300 seconds\n  PARENT_N = 95 (parent resolution)\n\n3. Implementation Procedure:\nInitialization:\n  - Start parent -95 points, n_pop0=20\n  - Read initial_h_values if provided (n=95)\n  - Create variation neighborhoods:\n        low_block = {h_block,strength=0.2}\n        high_block = {h_block,strength=0.8}\n  Selection Procedure:\n      def select_best_parent(best_quality, budget_remaining):\n          candidates = [(parent,n_points,n_budget)]\n          fitness = [evaluate(parent, n_points) - baseline]\n          # Select k such that k*n_time <= budget_remaining\n          if fitness[k] > ...:\n              return parent, n_points\n          ... \n      def repair_h(h, n_points):\n          h_clipped = np.clip(h, 0, 1)\n          total = np.sum(h_clipped)*dx - 1.0\n          if total == 0: return h_clipped\n          scale_factor = 1/tol if total<tol else (0.5*n_points*2.0)/total\n          h_corrected = h_clipped * scale_factor\n          # Final repair to ensure bounds and integral\n          return repair_again(h_corrected)\n\n  Operator Schemes:\n      Mutation: \n        def mutate(h):\n            decay = 0.2 (local mutation strength)\n            h_new = h * np.random.poisson(1.+decay, n_points)\n            ... scaling and repair\n      Crossover:\n        def crossover(parent1, parent2):\n            n, smoothness = values\n            hh = slice operations of variance s\n            h_new = underlying_gaussian_estimate(hh)\n            ... repair ensure bounds\n\n  Search Management:\n      budget_total = 1300 seconds\n      budget_overhead = 2 * time_per_evaluate\n      budget_renovation = 0.1 * budget_total\n      use_linux_related_delta = True\n      if use_linux_related_delta: \n          budget_renovation += 5 (adjust upward for time)\n\n      def evaluate_one_neighbor(h, n_points):\n          corr = np.correlate(h, 1-h, mode='full')\n          d2corr = dx_array if we have that else None\n          obj = np.max(corr) * (2.0/n_points)\n          # Score optimization moves specifically avoiding negative correlation shifts\n\n5. Compute Budget and Robustness:\n  Primary costs:\n      Time for correlation computation: O(n_points^2)\n      dominates over repair/selection costs\n  Budget Allocation:\n      monitoring_threshold = 140 seconds\n      rapid_restart at budget/2 if improvement stalls\n      if (curr_obj - best_obj)/best_obj > -0.01 or (elapsed_time % 50 < 1):\n          reshuffle_features()\n\n  Fallback Procedure:\n      valid_h = initial_h_values (if available)\n      fallback_fitness = compute_objective(valid_h, n_points)\n      if (candidate_fitness < fallback_fitness - 0.01):\n          return fallback_fitness, valid_h\n\n6. Validation and Return Contract:\n  Requirement checks:\n      1. Finite value for returned objective (catch np.inf/NaN)\n      2. h[i] between 0 and 1 for all i\n      3. hasattr(h_column, 'clip') ensuring the returned vector is repairable\n  Active checks:\n      def validate_objective(h):\n          if not isinstance(h, np.ndarray): raise TypeMismatchError\n          corr = np.full(2*n-1, np.inf)\n          corr_val = [np.correlate(h[i],1-h[i],mode='full') for ...]\n          # Verify specific lag behavior (edge non-zero)\n      Return format (obj, h, n_points)",
